# Waybill Totals / Charge Basis

## Canonical code

Use `kit_seed_normalize_charge_basis()` + `kit_seed_total_from_charge_basis()` in
`includes/sync/kit-charge-basis.php`. Do not reimplement mass/volume/max inline in
seed, PDF, JS, list, or verification — call or port that helper.

## Freight total rules

1. Sheet/DB columns: Z `mass_charge`, AA `volume_charge`, AB `charge_basis`.
2. `charge_basis` = mass/weight → billed freight = `mass_charge`.
3. `charge_basis` = volume → billed freight = `volume_charge`.
4. `charge_basis` empty / auto / max / higher / best → billed freight =
   `max(mass_charge, volume_charge)`.
5. Never default empty basis to `MASS` or `VOLUME` on seed/upsert — leave empty
   so rule 4 applies.
6. Rules 1–5 give **freight only**, not the billed total.
7. Sheet `product_invoice_amount` = parcels total → `waybill_items_total`.

## Billed total (`product_invoice_amount`)

DB `product_invoice_amount` is the **billed total**: freight (rules above) + VAT +
misc + SAD500/SADC. It is what List/UI Total / Cost shows.

1. Only `KIT_Bulletproof_Calculator::calculate_waybill_total()` produces it, reached
   via `KIT_Waybills::doubleCalcWaybillTotal()`. Never assemble the total by hand.
2. `vat_include` = true → VAT (10% of `waybill_items_total`) is part of the total.
   Freight alone is the wrong figure; that bug left 744 live waybills short by
   R 1.25m.
3. Never seed/write `product_invoice_amount` from a sheet cell or from freight
   alone. The sheet has no VAT-inclusive column — VAT is added by us. Every seed
   path derives it after writing the charge columns and line items.
4. Verification must not assert `product_invoice_amount` == basis freight. Verify
   `mass_charge` / `volume_charge` / `charge_basis` (sheet-owned) instead.

## Debug first (DB before code)

Before changing display/PDF/seed for a wrong total, read DB `mass_charge`,
`volume_charge`, `charge_basis`, `product_invoice_amount`. If the UI matches the
DB, the issue is data (or upstream seed), not the renderer.

If basis is set to the zero side while the other charge has money, that is
data/mapping — not a missing max fallback.

## Google Sheet seed — customer display

Treat seeded `No Customer Data` as a mapping/join bug first, not missing sheet
data, unless the sheet row itself has no customer fields.

## Example

```text
Bad:  basis=MASS, mass=0, volume=38704 → Total R 0.00 (rules working; wrong basis)
Good: basis empty → Total 38704; or basis=VOLUME when only volume has charge
```
